{"name":"Commodore","hex":"#25476a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Commodore","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A male given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Commodore"}],"entries":[{"title":"Commodore (rank)","blocks":[{"text":"Commodore is a senior naval rank used in many navies which is equivalent to brigadier or brigadier general and air commodore. It is superior to a navy captain, but below a rear admiral. It either is regarded as the most junior of the flag officers rank or may not hold the jurisdiction of a flag officer at all depending on the officer's appointment. Non-English-speaking nations commonly use the rank of flotilla admiral, counter admiral, or senior captain as an equivalent, although counter admiral may also correspond to rear admiral lower half abbreviated as RDML."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commodore_(rank)"},{"title":"Commodore (Royal Navy)","blocks":[{"text":"Commodore (Cdre) is a rank of the Royal Navy above captain and below rear admiral. It has a NATO ranking code of OF-6. The rank is equivalent to brigadier in the British Army and the Royal Marines and to air commodore in the Royal Air Force. Commodore has been a substantive rank in the Royal Navy since only 1997. Until then the term denoted a functional position rather than a formal rank, being the title bestowed on the senior officer of a fleet of at least two naval vessels comprising an independent command."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Pennant_of_a_Commodore_%28Royal_Navy%29.svg/330px-Pennant_of_a_Commodore_%28Royal_Navy%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commodore_(Royal_Navy)"},{"title":"Commodore (United States)","blocks":[{"text":"Commodore was an early title and later a rank in the United States Navy, United States Coast Guard and also has been a rank in the United States Public Health Service Commissioned Corps and the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration Commissioned Officer Corps and its ancestor organizations. For over two centuries, the designation has been given varying levels of authority and formality."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commodore_(United_States)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Broad_Pennant_of_a_United_States_Navy_Commodore_1870.png/500px-Broad_Pennant_of_a_United_States_Navy_Commodore_1870.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Broad_Pennant_of_a_United_States_Navy_Commodore_1870.png/500px-Broad_Pennant_of_a_United_States_Navy_Commodore_1870.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Short lived Broad Pennant of a US Navy Commodore 1870-[9]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABroad_Pennant_of_a_United_States_Navy_Commodore_1870.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Grace_Hopper_being_promoted_to_Commodore.jpg/500px-Grace_Hopper_being_promoted_to_Commodore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Grace_Hopper_being_promoted_to_Commodore.jpg/1280px-Grace_Hopper_being_promoted_to_Commodore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Grace_Hopper_being_promoted_to_Commodore.jpg/500px-Grace_Hopper_being_promoted_to_Commodore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grace Hopper being promoted to the rank of commodore in 1983","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrace_Hopper_being_promoted_to_Commodore.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Commodore_Charles_F._Clark%2C_USN_%28covered%29